## Resolution

- `Spline::hermite` and the gated block implement the original cubic basis, neighbour-dependent analytic gradients and linear tails. Cubic controls share the pruned mapping and projections.
- Schema 2 replaces 0/1 with explicit refusals. Four external fixtures check forward/backward, an SGD step and exact artifact round trips.
- On 296935cd, following fast-test staging e9c3a9e5, **20 host tests** and both portable release rlibs passed on the NRL branch. No build or test ran on fast-test.
- The cubic block's maximum recorded reference error is 5.551115123125783e-17. Separate tests exercise two knots, exact knots, both tails, C1 continuity and independent input/coefficient differences; full-block differences cover every trainable parameter.
- Fixture regeneration was byte-identical (SHA-256 8ddb51724f78ad98ee9122f6331adb573c13de580f1bfb36264d2c055cca16dd). Dated evidence is `nrl/reports/hermite-f64-2026-10-26.json` and `hermite-check-2026-10-26.txt`.
- These are bias-free block results, not B-spline implementation, trained-model improvement or native execution. SVD and the general pipeline remain under 900.
